<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's Central Puerto Q2 net down to $6.7 mln.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Central Puerto Q2 net down to $6.7 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Period to June 30.</p>
<p>Net $6.7 million vs $9.2 million.</p>
<p>EPS $0.075 vs $0.104.</p>
<p>ADR $0.376 vs $0.522.</p>
<p>Revs $82.0 million vs $84.0 million.  </p>
<p>NOTE: the company said at June 30 its net worth stood at $320.9 million.</p>
<p>A 31 percent stake of Central Puerto SA is in the hands of Chile's Chilgener SA, another 31 percent is shared by Chile's Chilquinta and  Pacifico Quinta Region, while the rest floats in Buenos Aires and, in the form of ADRs, in New York.</p>
<p>((--Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires newsroom, 541 318-0650))</p>
